Camille,<br />
<br />
I do not have it and I want to be precise about what that means, because "w=
e do not have it" and "it does not exist" are not the same statement and th=
e difference is going to matter.<br />
<br />
What SENTRY holds for examination 2011-0447 is two things. A summary record=
 - registrant, dates of fieldwork, examiner, disposition code C-2, closed n=
o further action - and a scanned copy of the closing letter of June 28, 201=
1. That is the entire file. There are no work papers, no correspondence, no=
 deficiency letter and no attachments.<br />
<br />
That is not because the examination had none. It is because of the 2016 mig=
ration. Examinations closed before January 1, 2014 migrated as summary plus=
 final letters only; correspondence and work papers were out of scope. Ever=
y pre-2014 examination in this office looks like this.<br />
<br />
So I cannot tell you whether a deficiency letter was issued in 2011. What I=
 can tell you is that if one was issued, SENTRY would not have it either wa=
y, and the record we produced to Respondent is not evidence that nothing ha=
ppened. It is evidence of what survived a migration.<br />
